  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "snoop: Error before allocation if a pseudo-header size is too large",
  "description": "In the Shomiti/Finisar Surveyor flavor of the snoop format, the\npseudo-header is variable length and given in the header. If the\npseudo-header length is larger than the total packet length, go\nahead and fail with an error instead of allocating a very large\nBuffer after integer overflow, and then failing to read bytes.\n\nThat Buffer is freed shortly afterwards with the failure, so this\nnear-4GiB allocation is only a problem for systems that might fail\nto make the allocation.\n\nUse checked integer arithmetic, and make the header length unsigned.\n\nThanks to AISLE Security for the report and PoC.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-08-02T23:01:47.360Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-08-03T15:06:47.514Z",
